{"title":"1981 AHSME Problems/Problem 18","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_18\">Problem 18</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 18\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The number of real solutions to the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/d/ffd7dd7000b0ad3abb2f5ebbaf6410580abd6bc6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{x}{100}=\\sin x\\]\" width=\"88\" height=\"33\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/1/881ee116d64a729b63111ac7d0afb01a2bf3d748.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 61\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 62\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 63\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 64\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 65$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"394\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The answer to this problem is the number of intersections between the graph of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/c/1bc9eec47d628562a54108d1717ea9298415c317.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = \\sin x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/1/c7126868a6d8fbae5817a13d03482e44376a7dcd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = \\frac{1}{100}x.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"108\" height=\"38\" /> We can do the right side of the coordinate plane first. Each cycle of the sine wave, consisting of 2π, will have 2 intersections (From the positive part of the sine wave) The line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/5/745005e61a90a7ecde2d3712828fef1dc7a57f4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = \\frac{1}{100}x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"103\" height=\"38\" /> will consist of 16 cycles plus a little bit extra for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> from 1 to 100. However, the extra is not complete enough to have any intersection at all. Thus, the number of intersections is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/0/2a0a8e2714cd666c322dce08b1b4601b0d79c072.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot 16 = 32.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"90\" height=\"14\" /> Because of symmetry, we can multiply by two to account for the left side, and subtract one because of the origin. So the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/f/0afabf85d38d47357e22d8233fea35c90066ca43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32 \\cdot 2 - 1 =  \\textbf{(C)}\\ 63.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"155\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.desmos.com/calculator/z6edqwu1kx\">https://www.desmos.com/calculator/z6edqwu1kx</a> - Graph\n</p><p><br />\n~Eric X\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_AHSME\" title=\"1981 AHSME\">1981 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1981 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1981 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1981\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"1981 AHSME Problems/Problem 17\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"1981 AHSME Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1981 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1981 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1981 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1981 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1981 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1981 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1981 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1981 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1981 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1981_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1981 AHSME Problems/Problem 